  <div class="body">
    <h2><span class="num">Reason 1</span>The bug spray you've been using might be more dangerous than the ticks.</h2>
    <figure class="fig"><div class="frame"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/1009/5601/2725/files/hf_20260611_220047_c6b954ec-7b98-4613-91bc-5346a08248b6.png?v=1781215545&width=1400" alt="Conventional bug spray." loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1400" height="1400"></div></figure>
    <p>DEET is a solvent strong enough to melt fishing line — and it only rides your skin for a few hours.</p>
    <p>Permethrin is worse: a pesticide the EPA calls <em>"likely carcinogenic,"</em> made for clothing, never your skin.</p>
    <div class="r-link">👉 <a href="https://pinemoor.co/products/double-potency-upgrade-ultimate-tick-protection-1-bottle?view=pinemoor-v2">See what I replaced it with</a></div>
    <div class="break"><span>· · ·</span></div>
    <h2><span class="num">Reason 2</span>Ticks Hunt By Questing. The Compounds In Pinemoor Stop That</h2>
    <figure class="fig"><div class="frame"><img src="{{ 'pm-ezgif-com-video-to-gif-e7b22.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="A tick questing in the grass." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="600" height="450"></div></figure>
    <p>A tick is blind. It finds you by the CO₂ you breathe and the scent off your skin.</p>
    <p>A spray only masks one patch — so the tick crawls to a spot you missed. <strong>Pinemoor changes the scent off your whole body, so it finds nothing.</strong></p>
    <div class="r-link">👉 <a href="https://pinemoor.co/products/double-potency-upgrade-ultimate-tick-protection-1-bottle?view=pinemoor-v2">Stop smelling like a host</a></div>
    <div class="break"><span>· · ·</span></div>
